    <entry>
        <title>Firefox is falling behind (not in market share)</title>
        <link href="https://blog.velocifyer.com/Posts/0,1,2025-8-9,Firefox+is+falling+behind.html"/>
        <id>https://blog.velocifyer.com/Posts/0,1,2025-8-9,Firefox+is+falling+behind.html</id>
        <!-- 1-based index unfortunately -->
        <updated>2025-09-12T16:04:00-04:00</updated>
        <summary>TLDR: Firefox is not implementing new web standards</summary>
        <content type="html">
            &lt;!doctype html&gt;
                        &lt;html lang=&quot;en-US&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;head&gt;
                                &lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;title&gt;Firefox is falling behind (not in market share)&lt;/title&gt;
                                &lt;link href=&quot;https://blog.velocifyer.com/Assets/Fonts/Noto/Sans/2025-8-3/file.css&quot; rel=&quot;stylesheet&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;link rel=&quot;icon&quot; href=&quot;https://blog.velocifyer.com/Assets/Images/spacetoad.jpg&quot; type=&quot;image/jpeg&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;!-- This uses a AGPL licensed backend, email velocifyer at velocifyer.com for the code and license --&gt;
                                &lt;meta
                                    name=&quot;description&quot;
                                    content=&quot;TLDR: Firefox is not implementing new web standards&quot;
                                &gt;
                                &lt;meta name=&quot;darkreader-lock&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;/head&gt;
                            &lt;body&gt;
                                &lt;h3&gt;2025-8-9 (September 10th, 2025)&lt;/h3&gt;
                                &lt;h4&gt;TLDR: Firefox is not implementing new web standards&lt;/h4&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;
                                    &lt;!-- TODO: fix line spacing --&gt;
                                    Firefox is a great browser, but it's not implementing new web standards.&lt;br&gt;
                                    I want to use WebUSB and WebSerial to flash devices, but Firefox won't let me.&lt;br&gt;
                                    I want to use Speculation Rules to reduce latency, but Firefox won't let me.&lt;br&gt;
                                &lt;/p&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;
                                    Because of Firefox not supporting new web standards, users will switch to the much worse chromium.
                                &lt;/p&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;
                                    Here is an incomplete list of things that are missing from Firefox that are in Chromium:
                                    &lt;ul&gt;                         &lt;!-- TODO: make this part condensed --&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;WebUSB and WebSerial (the reason it is missing is a alleged security risk for people who ignore warnings)&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Speculation Rules&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Certain referer policies&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;User-Agent Client Hints API&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;WebGPU (outside of Microsoft Losedows)&lt;/li&gt;
                                    &lt;/ul&gt;
                                &lt;/p&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;
                                    Here is an incomplete list of things missing in Firefox that are not in Chromium ranked by usefulness:
                                    &lt;ol start=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;JPEG XL&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;0-based index on ordered lists by default&lt;/li&gt;
                                    &lt;/ol&gt;
                                &lt;/p&gt;
                                &lt;hr&gt;
                                &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45202715&quot;&gt;First Hacker News post&lt;/a&gt;
                                &lt;hr&gt;
                                &lt;small&gt;
                                    Except for the favicon and javascript and the font, this is licensed CC-BY-SA 4.0 𝕍𝕖𝕝𝕠𝕔𝕚𝕗𝕪𝕖𝕣.&lt;br&gt;
                                    The font used on this website is Noto Sans, which uses &lt;a href=&quot;/Assets/Fonts/Noto/Sans/2025-8-3/License.txt&quot;&gt;this license&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
                                    This blog is avalible on &lt;a href=&quot;https://codeberg.org/Velocifyer/Blog-ifyer&quot;&gt;Codeberg&lt;/a&gt;. Make a issue or merge request if it would be useful.&lt;br&gt;
                                    We have not knowingly sent logs of blog-ifyer to third parties. Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://files.velocifyer.com/Warant%20canaries/&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer-when-downgrade&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to get PGP signed canaries. See Cloudflare's warranty canary &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/transparency/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;
