    <entry>
        <title>0-based indexes are the best</title>
        <link href="https://blog.velocifyer.com/Posts/0,2,2025-8-10,0-based-indexes+are+the+best.html"/>
        <id>https://blog.velocifyer.com/Posts/0,2,2025-8-10,0-based-indexes+are+the+best.html</id>
        <!-- 1-based index unfortunately -->
        <updated>2025-09-12T16:20:00-04:00</updated>
        <summary>Here's why you should use 0-based indexes</summary>
        <content type="html">
            &lt;!doctype html&gt;
                        &lt;html lang=&quot;en-US&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;head&gt;
                                &lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;title&gt;0-Based indexes are the best&lt;/title&gt;
                                &lt;link href=&quot;https://files.velocifyer.com/Warant%20canaries/&quot; rel=&quot;dns-prefetch&quot;&gt;
                                &lt;meta
                                    name=&quot;description&quot;
                                    content=&quot;Here's why you should use 0-based indexes&quot;
                                &gt;
                                &lt;meta name=&quot;darkreader-lock&quot;&gt;
                            &lt;/head&gt;
                            &lt;body&gt;
                                &lt;h3&gt;2025-8-10 (September 11th, 2025)&lt;/h3&gt;
                                &lt;h4&gt;TLDR: use 0-based indexes now and in the future (and in the past if you can)&lt;/h4&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;
                                    &lt;!-- TODO: fix line spacing --&gt;
                                    I get so annoyed when indexes aren't 0-based. &lt;br&gt;
                                    Indexes should be 0-based. A 1-based index confuses me (and many other people) because i'm used to 0-based indexes, and so are many people.&lt;br&gt;
                                    That's why i write 11th september 2025 as &quot;2025-8-10&quot;
                                &lt;/p&gt;
                                &lt;p&gt;Here is what a 0 based index looks like:&lt;/p&gt;
                                    &lt;ol start=&quot;0&quot;&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Blog-ifyer&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Pasta&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Hot dogs&lt;/li&gt;
                                    &lt;/ol&gt;
                                Here is what a 1 based index looks like:
                                    &lt;ol start=&quot;1&quot;&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Blog-ifyer&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Pasta&lt;/li&gt;
                                        &lt;li&gt;Hot dogs&lt;/li&gt;
                                    &lt;/ol&gt;
                                    At least dont use 0.5 based indexes.
                                &lt;hr&gt;
                                    &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=45221920&quot;&gt;First Hacker News post (The people there incorrectly think i'm trolling)&lt;/a&gt;
                                &lt;hr&gt;
                                &lt;small&gt;
                                    This is licensed CC-BY-SA 4.0 𝕍𝕖𝕝𝕠𝕔𝕚𝕗𝕪𝕖𝕣.&lt;br&gt;
                                    This blog is avalible on &lt;a href=&quot;https://codeberg.org/Velocifyer/Blog-ifyer&quot;&gt;Codeberg&lt;/a&gt;. Make a issue or merge request if it would be useful.&lt;br&gt;
                                    I have not knowingly sent logs of blog-ifyer to third parties. Click &lt;a href=&quot;https://files.velocifyer.com/Warant%20canaries/&quot; referrerpolicy=&quot;no-referrer-when-downgrade&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to get PGP signed canaries. See Cloudflare's warranty canary &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudflare.com/transparency/&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;
